---
layout: base.njk
title: "The corpus"
description: "Everything Elixir MCP has recorded: battles, players, clans, war weeks and daily snapshots, how often each is collected, and how long it is kept. Aggregates are public by design."
permalink: /data/index.html
canonical: /data
navActive: data
---
{#-
  The corpus proof, and the reason this page is a real document rather
  than a screen in the app: an aggregate is public by design, and a
  crawler, an agent and a person who has not signed in should all be able
  to read it. Everything here is baked at deploy from /api/public/stats,
  except one live strip that says so.
-#}
{%- set t = stats.totals %}
{%- set n = "—" %}

<div class="siterail">
  {#- Data stays ONE document: a reader comparing totals against the
      growth curve should not have to navigate. So the rail scrolls
      rather than swapping views; rail-anchors.js marks where you are. -#}
  <nav class="siterail__nav" aria-label="On this page" data-rail-anchors>
    <div class="rail__group">On this page</div>
    <a class="rail__item" href="#totals">Corpus totals</a>
    <a class="rail__item" href="#growth">Growth over time</a>
    <a class="rail__item" href="#collect">What we collect</a>
    <a class="rail__item" href="#now">Recording now</a>
    <a class="rail__item" href="#machines">For machines</a>
    <div class="siterail__foot">
      <a class="btn btn--sm" href="/data/changelog">Contract changelog</a>
      <a class="btn btn--sm" href="/status/service">Status console</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="siterail__body">
<div class="page-head" style="align-items: flex-end">
  <div>
    <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 6px">The corpus</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin: 0; max-width: 58ch">
      Everything Elixir has recorded. Aggregates are public by design; what
      belongs to an account never is.
    </p>
  </div>
  <span class="mono" style="margin-left: auto; text-align: right; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-faint)">
    {% if t %}as of {{ t.newest_battle | stamp }}{% else %}awaiting the next build{% endif %}<br />rebuilt on every deploy
  </span>
</div>

{#- Five totals. This is the ONE place a number is gold: a brand moment
    on the marketing half, not a reading in the console. -#}
<div class="stats" id="totals" style="margin-bottom: 22px">
  <div class="stats__cell">
    <div class="label">battles</div>
    <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.battles | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="stats__note">{% if t %}{{ t.oldest_battle | day }} → {{ t.newest_battle | day }}{% else %}recorded{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="stats__cell">
    <div class="label">players</div>
    <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.players | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="stats__note">observed{% if t %} · {{ t.players_recording | number }} recorded{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="stats__cell">
    <div class="label">clans</div>
    <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.clans | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="stats__note">observed{% if t %} · {{ t.clans_recording | number }} recorded{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="stats__cell">
    <div class="label">war weeks</div>
    <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.war_weeks | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="stats__note">past the API&rsquo;s 20-week window</div>
  </div>
  <div class="stats__cell">
    <div class="label">snapshots</div>
    <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.snapshots | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="stats__note">daily player snapshots</div>
  </div>
</div>

{#- Cumulative battles by month, computed at build time from the daily
    series. A month with no battles is a real zero on the axis: the shape
    of the corpus is part of the truth, so nothing is compressed. -#}
{%- set curve = stats.series.battles_daily | cumulativeByMonth %}
{% if not curve.points %}
<section class="panel" id="growth" style="margin-bottom: 22px">
  <div class="panel__head"><span>The corpus keeps growing</span></div>
  <div class="panel__body footnote">The growth curve is drawn from the daily series at build time; this build had no series to draw from.</div>
</section>
{% endif %}
{% if curve.points %}
<section class="panel" id="growth" style="margin-bottom: 22px">
  <div class="panel__head">
    <span>The corpus keeps growing</span>
    <span class="footnote" style="border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 2px 8px; font-weight: 400">battles, cumulative</span>
    <span class="footnote" style="border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 2px 8px; font-weight: 400">monthly · UTC</span>
  </div>
  <div style="padding: 18px 18px 8px">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 700 168" style="width: 100%; height: auto; display: block" role="img"
         aria-label="Battles recorded, cumulative, by month, {{ curve.first }} to {{ curve.last }}">
      <line x1="20" x2="640" y1="140" y2="140" stroke="var(--line)"></line>
      <line x1="20" x2="640" y1="76" y2="76" stroke="var(--line-soft)" stroke-dasharray="2 5"></line>
      <line x1="20" x2="640" y1="12" y2="12" stroke="var(--line-soft)" stroke-dasharray="2 5"></line>
      <path d="{{ curve.area }}" fill="rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.2)"></path>
      <path d="{{ curve.line }}" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent-bright)" stroke-width="2.5"></path>
      <circle cx="{{ curve.tipX }}" cy="{{ curve.tipY }}" r="4" fill="var(--accent-bright)"></circle>
      <text x="648" y="16" fill="var(--ink-faint)" font-size="11" font-family="ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace">{{ curve.top }}</text>
      <text x="648" y="80" fill="var(--ink-faint)" font-size="11" font-family="ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace">{{ curve.half }}</text>
      {%- for m in curve.points %}
      <text x="{{ m.x }}" y="158" fill="var(--ink-faint)" font-size="11" font-family="ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace" text-anchor="middle">{{ m.label }}</text>
      {%- endfor %}
    </svg>
  </div>
  <div class="panel__foot" style="font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-dim)">
    Battles are bucketed by when they were <em style="color: var(--ink-body)">played</em>, not when we
    recorded them, so a backfilled archive lands in its own month rather than
    the day it arrived. The newest month is partial. Full history is deliberate
    today; a retention policy comes as the corpus grows, and it will be
    published here.
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="panel" id="collect" style="margin-bottom: 22px">
  <div class="panel__head">
    <span>What we collect</span>
    <a style="margin-left: auto; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 400" href="/docs/recording">How recording works ›</a>
  </div>
  <div class="table__scroll">
    <table class="table" style="min-width: 620px">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>WHAT</th>
          <th>HOW OFTEN</th>
          <th>SINCE</th>
          <th>KEPT</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Player battle logs</td>
          <td>every 5&ndash;30 min while active</td>
          <td>{% if t %}{{ t.oldest_battle | day }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</td>
          <td>full history today</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Player profiles</td>
          <td>daily snapshot</td>
          <td>{% if t %}{{ t.oldest_battle | day }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</td>
          <td>full history today</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Clans</td>
          <td>every 15 min</td>
          <td>{% if t %}{{ t.oldest_battle | day }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</td>
          <td>full history today</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>River races (clan wars)</td>
          <td>weekly, corrected as the race runs</td>
          <td>{% if t %}{{ t.oldest_battle | day }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</td>
          <td>full history today</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Decks, cards, matchups</td>
          <td>derived from recorded battles</td>
          <td>&mdash;</td>
          <td>recomputed</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="panel__foot" style="font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-dim)">
    Recording is requested per player and per clan by the people who own them.
    Raw payloads are kept about 60 days; the canonical record is not rebuilt
    from them. Account data is never public.
  </div>
</section>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap">
  {#- The only live element on the page. With JavaScript off it shows the
      deploy-time values and still reads true, which is why the numbers
      are rendered server-side and only replaced if the fetch succeeds. -#}
  <section class="panel" id="now" style="flex: 1 1 340px; border-color: var(--ok-edge)">
    <div class="panel__body">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 11px">
        <span class="chip chip--ok"><span class="chip__dot"></span>recording</span>
        <span style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600">Right now</span>
        <span class="mono" style="margin-left: auto; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-faint)">live · cached 60s</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 22px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-body)">
        <span>last battle <strong data-live="last" style="color: var(--ink)">{% if t %}{{ t.newest_battle | day }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</strong></span>
        <span><strong data-live="hour" style="color: var(--ink)">{{ n }}</strong> this hour</span>
        <span><strong data-live="collectors" style="color: var(--ink)">{% if t %}{{ t.collectors_active }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</strong> collectors</span>
      </div>
      <p class="footnote" style="margin: 11px 0 0">
        Operators get the whole picture in the <a href="/status/service">console&rsquo;s status page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="machines" style="flex: 1 1 250px">
    <div class="panel__body">
      <div style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 11px">Read it as a machine</div>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px">
        <a class="mono" href="/api/public/stats">/api/public/stats</a>
        <a class="mono" href="/api/public/status">/api/public/status</a>
        <a class="mono" href="/tools.json">/tools.json</a>
        <a class="mono" href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>
        <a class="mono" href="/feed.xml">/feed.xml</a>
      </div>
      <p class="footnote" style="margin: 12px 0 0">
        No key needed for any of these. The recorded history itself needs an
        account, over <a href="/docs/protocol">MCP</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<p class="footnote" style="margin: 22px 0 0; max-width: 78ch">
  The full daily charts, with every collector broken out, live in the
  <a href="/data/dashboard">daily corpus charts</a>. The tool contract&rsquo;s own
  history is the <a href="/data/changelog">changelog</a>.
</p>
  </div>
</div>

<script defer src="/assets/data-live.js"></script>
<script defer src="/assets/rail-anchors.js"></script>
